# ARPL: when the destination selector's RPL is below the source's, raise it
# to the source RPL and set ZF; otherwise ZF=0 and the selector stays.
# Protected mode only (the decoder refuses it in real mode, where 63h is
# #UD). A memory destination is written only when the RPL changes: the
# 386 does not write back an unchanged selector, so a read-only segment
# faults only then (test386 POST 17h).
require_protected_mode
$INPUT
read source src 16
const m3 16 3
and dst_rpl selector m3
and src_rpl source m3
ult raise dst_rpl src_rpl
const clear_rpl 16 65532
and kept selector clear_rpl
or adjusted kept src_rpl
select result raise adjusted selector
$OUTPUT
flag ZF raise
preserve_flags remaining
retire
